book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd straightway Jesus constrained his disciples to get into a ship, and to go before him unto the other side, while he sent the multitudes away.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And when he had sent the multitudes away, he went up into a mountain apart to pray: and when the evening was come, he was there alone.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[But the ship was now in the midst of the sea, tossed with waves: for the wind was contrary.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNAnd in the fourth watch of the night Jesus went unto them, walking on the sea.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And when the disciples saw him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, It is a spirit; and they cried out for fear.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXBut straightway Jesus spake unto them, saying, Be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYAnd Peter answered him and said, Lord, if it be thou, bid me come unto thee on the water.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhAnd he said, Come. And when Peter was come down out of the ship, he walked on the water, to go to Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkBut when he saw the wind boisterous, he was afraid; and beginning to sink, he cried, saying, Lord, save me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And immediately Jesus stretched forth his hand, and caught him, and said unto him, O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ7And when they were come into the ship, the wind ceased.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdThen they that were in the ship came and worshipped him, saying, Of a truth thou art the Son of God.¦layout ªlast_verse!…¤book'§chapter«first_verse"ªlast_verse$¦verses“„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙDAnd when they were gone over, they came into the land of Gennesaret.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And when the men of that place had knowledge of him, they sent out into all that country round about, and brought unto him all that were diseased;¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuand besought him that they might only touch the hem of his garment: and as many as touched were made perfectly whole.¦layout ªlast_verse$